  "article": {
    "id": "re-foundations-4a-i-ve-found-the-titanic",
    "title": "RE Foundations / 4A / I’ve Found the Titanic!",
    "text_type": "informational",
    "audience": {
      "grade_band": "upper_elementary"
    },
    "language": "en"
  },
  "content": {
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "As a boy, Robert Ballard liked to read about shipwrecks."
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "He read a lot about the Titanic."
          },
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "“My lifelong dream was to find this great ship,” he says."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "On August 31, 1985, Ballard’s dream came true."
          },
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "He found the wreck of the Titanic."
          },
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "The ship was in two main parts, lying four kilometers under the sea."
          },
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "Using video cameras and an undersea robot, 1 Ballard looked around the ship."
          },
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "He found many items that told the sad story of the Titanic’s end."
          },
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "For example, he found a child’s shoes, a reminder of the many deaths that happened that night in 1912."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "order": 3,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "In 1986, Ballard visited the Titanic again."
          },
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "This time, he reached the ship in a small submarine."
          },
          {
            "id": "s12",
            "text": "A deep-sea robot took photos inside the ship."
          },
          {
            "id": "s13",
            "text": "When other people saw the photos, they wanted to visit the ship, too."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "order": 4,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s14",
            "text": "When Ballard returned in 2004, he found the Titanic in very bad condition."
          },
          {
            "id": "s15",
            "text": "Other explorers had taken away about 6,000 items, like clothes, dishes, and shoes."
          },
          {
            "id": "s16",
            "text": "Some even took pieces of the ship."
          },
          {
            "id": "s17",
            "text": "They think these things should be moved to a safer place, but Ballard doesn’t agree."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "order": 5,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s18",
            "text": "Ballard believes that taking things from the Titanic is wrong."
          },
          {
            "id": "s19",
            "text": "Instead, he wants to put lights and cameras on and around the shipwreck."
          },
          {
            "id": "s20",
            "text": "This way, people can see the great ship and remember what happened to it."
          },
          {
            "id": "s21",
            "text": "“As long as she needs protection,” 3 says Ballard, “the Titanic will always be part of my life.”"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
